<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Timor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> (Timor-Leste) is a country occupying the eastern half of the island of Timor in South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. It was a Portuguese colony for centuries and one of the last remnants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>; after Portugal withdrew in 1975 it was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> and became independent in 2002. Portuguese remains an official language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-timor.jpg" alt="East Timor" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history, below, for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_East_Timor.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
